    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "When a mathematics teacher was asked her age she replied, ‘One-fifth of my age three years ago, when added to half my age last year, gives my age 11 years ago.’ How old is she?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "33 years old.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the teacher’s present age in years.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x-3}{5}+\\frac{x-1}{2}&=x-11\\\\2(x-3)+5(x-1)&=10(x-11)\\\\2x-6+5x-5&=10x-110\\\\7x-11&=10x-110\\\\99&=3x\\\\x&=33\\end{align*}$$\nThe teacher is 33 years old. Check: one-fifth of 30 plus half of 32 is $6+16=22$, her age 11 years ago.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
